# Keep working-tree bytes identical to the stored blob, everywhere.
#
# Specification/Evidence/ binds TcUnit runtime results to sources by SHA-256, and
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system config. With no
# attributes file, a fresh clone materialises CRLF working-tree files whose
# hashes no longer match the recorded ones — every evidence record would fail to
# verify on any machine but the one that wrote it, silently and with no error.
#
# TwinCAT source is XML the IDE rewrites in place, so end-of-line normalisation
# is churn there too. Byte fidelity is what this repository needs; text
# conversion is what it must not have.
* -text
